((intellect3-science
  ((question . "In the neoclassical growth model equation:  \n\\[\n\\text{Potential output growth} = 1.5 + 0.72(\\text{Growth of labor}) + 0.28(\\text{Growth of capital}),\n\\]  \nthe coefficient on the growth rate of labor (0.72) is best interpreted as:")
    (answer . "0.72")
    (domain . "economics")
    (difficulty . "0.375"))
  ((question . "In the circuit of Prob. 24-167, an 8.0-H, 4.0-Ω coil is connected in series with a 2.0-Ω resistor, a 6.0-V battery, and a switch. If the 2.0-Ω resistor is to be replaced by another resistor to achieve a time constant of 1/3 s, determine the resistance value of the new resistor.")
    (answer . "20")
    (domain . "physics")
    (difficulty . "0.062"))
  ((question . "A block slides up an inclined plane with an initial velocity \\( v \\). The plane makes an angle \\( \\alpha \\) with the horizontal, and the coefficient of friction is \\( \\mu \\). Derive the distance \\( s \\) the block travels before coming to rest, given the work-energy principle:\n\\[\n- mgs \\sin \\alpha - \\mu mg s \\cos \\alpha = 0 - \\frac{1}{2} mv^2.\n\\]\nSimplify the expression for \\( s \\) and calculate its value when \\( v = l \\), \\( \\alpha = 30^\\circ \\), and \\( \\mu = \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{3}} \\).")
    (answer . "5")
    (domain . "physics")
    (difficulty . "0.062"))
  ((question . "A gas is compressed from a volume of 200 cc to 50 cc at a constant pressure of \\(10^5\\) Pa. Calculate the work done on the gas during this compression. If no heat is transferred during the process (adiabatic), what is the change in internal energy of the gas?")
    (answer . "4.5")
    (domain . "chemistry")
    (difficulty . "0.25"))
  ((question . "The average demand for a particular type of pump is 2.8 pumps per week, and demand occurs randomly and independently. The current stock is 1 pump. If supplies are ordered on Tuesday morning and arrive on Friday morning (a 3-day interval), what is the probability that the stock will be exhausted and there will be unsatisfied demand for at least one pump by Friday morning?")
    (answer . "0.3374")
    (domain . "chemistry")
    (difficulty . "0.375"))
  ((question . "For an antireflective coating on a glass lens (\\( n_2 = 1.5 \\)) at normal incidence, what should the index of refraction \\( n_1 \\) of the coating be to achieve zero reflectivity? Assume the incident medium is air (\\( n_0 = 1 \\)) and \\( n_1 < n_2 \\).")
    (answer . "1.24")
    (domain . "physics")
    (difficulty . "0.125"))
  ((question . "What is the optimal relative humidity for grown poultry birds?")
    (answer . "50%")
    (domain . "biology")
    (difficulty . "0.188"))
  ((question . "Dry ice is solid carbon dioxide. A 0.050 g sample of dry ice is placed in an evacuated 4.6 L vessel at 30°C. Calculate the pressure inside the vessel after all the dry ice has been converted to CO₂ gas.")
    (answer . "0.00614")
    (domain . "physics")
    (difficulty . "0.438"))
  ((question . "An electric heating coil is immersed in a stirred tank. The shaft work of the stirrer is 560 W. A solvent at 15°C with a heat capacity of 2.1 J/g °C is fed into the tank at a rate of 15 kg/h. Heated solvent is discharged at the same flow rate. The tank is filled initially with 125 kg cold solvent at 10°C. The rate of heating the electric coil is 2000 W. Calculate the time required for the temperature of the solvent to reach 60°C.")
    (answer . "5521")
    (domain . "chemistry")
    (difficulty . "0.062"))
  ((question . "A dealer quotes an annual interest rate of 5.3% for a 5-year deposit with interest paid once per year. Assuming that interim interest payments can be reinvested at the same rate, what equivalent rate should the dealer quote if the customer prefers to receive the interest quarterly?")
    (answer . "5.198%")
    (domain . "economics")
    (difficulty . "0.062"))
))
